WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.222
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.522 --> 00:00:09.408
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:16.749
Unit nineteen: Indefinite Pronouns (someone/anything). Today you will talk about unknown or general people and things.

4
00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:19.759
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.794
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:25.605
Someone.

7
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:28.825
Someone means a person that we do not name.

8
00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:30.963
Someone is at the door.

9
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.144
Your turn. Say: Someone.

10
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.071
Someone.

11
00:00:38.817 --> 00:00:39.597
Anyone.

12
00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:44.173
Anyone means any person, used in questions and negatives.

13
00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:45.947
Is anyone here?

14
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.947
Your turn. Say: Anyone.

15
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:52.720
Anyone.

16
00:00:53.483 --> 00:00:54.299
Something.

17
00:00:55.283 --> 00:00:57.480
Something means a thing that we do not name.

18
00:00:58.083 --> 00:00:59.607
I need something to drink.

19
00:01:00.217 --> 00:01:02.753
Your turn. Say: Something.

20
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:06.555
Something.

21
00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:08.202
Anything.

22
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:12.366
Anything means any thing, used in questions and negatives.

23
00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.357
I don't need anything.

24
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:17.463
Your turn. Say: Anything.

25
00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.220
Anything.

26
00:01:21.983 --> 00:01:22.810
Nobody.

27
00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.503
Nobody means no person.

28
00:01:26.117 --> 00:01:27.745
Nobody knows the answer.

29
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.793
Your turn. Say: Nobody.

30
00:01:33.633 --> 00:01:34.495
Nobody.

31
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.158
Nothing.

32
00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.685
Nothing means no thing.

33
00:01:39.283 --> 00:01:40.807
There is nothing in the box.

34
00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:43.930
Your turn. Say: Nothing.

35
00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:47.745
Nothing.

36
00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:49.461
Everyone.

37
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.124
Everyone means all people.

38
00:01:52.717 --> 00:01:54.008
Everyone is here.

39
00:01:54.617 --> 00:01:57.072
Your turn. Say: Everyone.

40
00:01:59.933 --> 00:02:01.016
Everyone.

41
00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:02.751
Everything.

42
00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.541
Everything means all things.

43
00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.534
Everything is ready.

44
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.524
Your turn. Say: Everything.

45
00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.252
Everything.

46
00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:18.717
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:23.385
Visal, someone is at the door. How do we say we do not know who?

48
00:02:24.483 --> 00:02:36.865
We use someone. Indefinite pronouns talk about people or things that are not named: someone, something, anyone, anything, everyone, everything, nobody and nothing.

49
00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.857
When do we use some and any?

50
00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:55.522
Some in positive sentences: I need something. Any in questions and negatives: Is there anything to eat? I don't see anyone. No- forms are already negative: Nobody came. Do not add another negative.

51
00:02:56.617 --> 00:02:58.175
Do they take a singular verb?

52
00:02:59.283 --> 00:03:13.554
Yes, always: Everyone is happy. Nothing is impossible. Everything was fine. This surprises many learners, because everyone feels plural. Remember the grammar is singular.

53
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.084
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:21.759
Grammar focus: Indefinite pronouns: some- and any- and no- and every-.

55
00:03:22.059 --> 00:03:23.176
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.883 --> 00:03:25.349
Someone is at the door.

57
00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.983
I don't see anyone in the room.

58
00:03:28.883 --> 00:03:30.418
Everything is ready now.

59
00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:39.815
Use some- in positive sentences and any- in questions and negatives. No- words are already negative. All these pronouns take a singular verb.

60
00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:43.667
Be careful! Don't say: I don't see nobody.

61
00:03:45.633 --> 00:03:47.807
Say: I don't see anybody.

62
00:03:48.107 --> 00:03:49.689
Do not use a double negative.

63
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.164
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:54.956
Who and What?.

65
00:03:55.256 --> 00:03:57.360
Someone is at the door, but I don't know who.

66
00:03:58.367 --> 00:04:01.356
Is there anything to eat? There is nothing in the fridge.

67
00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:05.678
Nobody came to the party, so everyone was surprised.

68
00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.422
I don't see anyone here.

69
00:04:09.433 --> 00:04:11.909
Everything is ready, and everyone is happy.

70
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.118
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:17.983 --> 00:04:20.740
I don't know blank in this town. (negative)

72
00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:24.752
A, anyone. B, someone. C, nobody.

73
00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.079
The answer is A: anyone.

74
00:04:31.217 --> 00:04:33.915
There is blank in the box. It is empty.

75
00:04:34.215 --> 00:04:37.579
A, nothing. B, anything. C, something.

76
00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:42.703
The answer is A: nothing.

77
00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.315
Everyone blank here.

78
00:04:45.615 --> 00:04:48.700
A, are. B, is. C, were.

79
00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:53.930
The answer is B: is.

80
00:04:55.083 --> 00:04:56.735
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:57.035 --> 00:05:02.325
A, I don't see nobody.. B, I don't see anybody.. C, I see nobody not..

82
00:05:05.867 --> 00:05:08.737
The answer is B: I don't see anybody..

83
00:05:09.883 --> 00:05:12.150
According to the reading, what is there to eat?

84
00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:16.161
A, nothing in the fridge. B, rice. C, fruit.

85
00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:22.385
The answer is A: nothing in the fridge.

86
00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.682
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:27.517 --> 00:05:30.840
Write a sentence using 'someone' and a sentence using 'nothing'.

88
00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.081
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:41.381 --> 00:05:52.395
Someone left a bag in the classroom. There is nothing inside it, and nobody knows whose it is. I use someone for a person that I do not know and nothing for no thing.

90
00:05:52.695 --> 00:05:55.054
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:02.062
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and indefinite pronouns: some- and any- and no- and every-.

92
00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:06.071
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

93
00:06:06.371 --> 00:06:08.919
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

94
00:06:09.219 --> 00:06:12.324
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

